A||N||1||WhiteFieroBlur||What determines lowering height with springs?||||1||
Z||000000||WhiteFieroBlur||11-05-2001||11:45 PM||||Well after some hair pulling searching on lowering I have decided to just go with the Suspension Tech springs. I just can't afford them high dollar coils and spindles. Man I hate expensive stuff  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">. <P>OK now that I have what I want what I am confused about is how can everyone have different heights on the same set of springs? what determines how low it goes. I am scared that its gonna lower only an inch. Thats what the tech at JCWhitney says that they lower only 1 inch. But people on here said they lower 1.5 or even 2". <P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroJoe||11-06-2001||12:43 PM||||Don't have an exact answer, but tire size and rim size makes a difference, too.  What I've been told is that if you have a spring 2" shorter than stock, then you'll be lower 2".  But, that's also with springs that have the same spring rate (softness or hardness).  I imagine if you have a spring that's 2" shorter than stock, but a harder spring rate, that you might only get 1" of lowering.||||reg||1
